{"id":"marketplace","corpus":"aws","title":"AWS Marketplace","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/marketplace/latest/userguide/what-is-marketplace.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"AWS Marketplace"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS Marketplace is a curated digital catalog that customers can use to find, buy, deploy, and manage third-party software, data, and services to build solutions and run their businesses. AWS Marketplace includes thousands of software listings from popular categories such as security, business applications, machine learning, and data products across specific industries, such as healthcare, financial services, and telecommunications. Customers can quickly launch preconfigured software, and choose software solutions in Amazon Machine Images (AMIs), software as a service (SaaS), and other formats. Professional services are also available to help customers configure, deploy, and manage third-party software. For a complete list of delivery methods, see Product delivery."},{"kind":"p","text":"You can use AWS Marketplace as a buyer (subscriber), seller (provider), or both. Anyone with an AWS account can use AWS Marketplace as a buyer, and can register to become a seller. A seller can be an independent software vendor, channel partner, managed services provider, or individual with an AWS-compatible product or service."},{"kind":"p","text":"Data product providers must meet the AWS Data Exchange eligibility requirements. For more information, see Providing data products on AWS Data Exchange in the AWS Data Exchange User Guide."},{"kind":"p","text":"Eligible partners can programmatically list AWS Marketplace products outside of AWS Marketplace. For more information about becoming an eligible partner, contact your AWS Marketplace business development partner."},{"kind":"p","text":"The following video explains more about selling in AWS Marketplace."}],"lemmas":{"marketplaces":["marketplace","marketpla